[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186162120 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-da99206a-ee96-54b9-a8bb-1c95438c5559" "question-9a19ca23-6c60-5d6e-8799-38d55529cc16"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-da99206a-ee96-54b9-a8bb-1c95438c5559" :question/id #uuid "da99206a-ee96-54b9-a8bb-1c95438c5559" :question/math-academy-id "q-143850" :question/problem "Find $\\text{E}[4(X-1)],$ given that random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4},\\, & 1\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le {x}^{2}; \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables, and $f(x,y)$ is their joint probability density function. If $r:{R}^{2}\\to R$ is a function of two variables, then the rule of the lazy statistician states that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X,Y)]={∬}_{{R}^{2}}r(x,y)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=4(x-1).\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch the region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le {x}^{2}\\},$ where $f(x,y)$ is nonzero.\n\n![](images/bd/bd8d2d36a0fe570e6ccdb096c6c39bc9c9edeed9b008dada504801025055438f.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[4(X-1)] & ={∬}_{{R}^{2}}4(x-1)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}4(x-1)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{{x}^{2}}4(x-1)\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{2}(x-1){\\int }_{1}^{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{2}(x-1)[y]_{y=1}^{y={x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{2}(x-1)({x}^{2}-1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{2}({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+x]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =3[(4-\\frac{8}{3}-2+2)-(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}+1)] \\\\  & =3(\\frac{4}{3}-\\frac{5}{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4a370ffb-9f03-59b2-ac60-62d599bab917"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4a370ffb-9f03-59b2-ac60-62d599bab917" :answer-field/id #uuid "4a370ffb-9f03-59b2-ac60-62d599bab917" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d153fc31-a51b-5ff0-a56d-5400a28d1dca" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d153fc31-a51b-5ff0-a56d-5400a28d1dca" "answer-0b87866d-7ca3-5ffe-9bf1-7ca2dbed6087" "answer-0094f649-619d-53d4-bd4a-599974a79f65" "answer-88871071-0592-5a72-9ee4-9896fb71c1b1" "answer-617c7900-1787-5067-bf53-b914ea33d964"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d153fc31-a51b-5ff0-a56d-5400a28d1dca" :answer/id #uuid "d153fc31-a51b-5ff0-a56d-5400a28d1dca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b87866d-7ca3-5ffe-9bf1-7ca2dbed6087" :answer/id #uuid "0b87866d-7ca3-5ffe-9bf1-7ca2dbed6087" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0094f649-619d-53d4-bd4a-599974a79f65" :answer/id #uuid "0094f649-619d-53d4-bd4a-599974a79f65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88871071-0592-5a72-9ee4-9896fb71c1b1" :answer/id #uuid "88871071-0592-5a72-9ee4-9896fb71c1b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-617c7900-1787-5067-bf53-b914ea33d964" :answer/id #uuid "617c7900-1787-5067-bf53-b914ea33d964" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9a19ca23-6c60-5d6e-8799-38d55529cc16" :question/id #uuid "9a19ca23-6c60-5d6e-8799-38d55529cc16" :question/math-academy-id "q-143871" :question/problem "Find $\\text{E}[{(X+Y)}^{2}],$ given that random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4},\\, & y\\le x\\le 4-y,\\,0\\le y\\le 2; \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables, and $f(x,y)$ is their joint probability density function. If $r:{R}^{2}\\to R$ is a function of two variables, then the rule of the lazy statistician states that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X,Y)]={∬}_{{R}^{2}}r(x,y)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=(x+y)^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch the region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\le x\\le 4-y,\\,0\\le y\\le 2\\},$ where $f(x,y)$ is nonzero.\n\n![](images/8d/8d1935944ffa0017da736fc540ff823df8a052c2c32c985553cde08ea5fce8da.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{(X+Y)}^{2}] & ={∬}_{{R}^{2}}(x+y)^{2}\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(x+y)^{2}\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y}^{4-y}(x+y)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{3}(x+y)^{3}]}_{x=y}^{x=4-y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[\\frac{1}{3}(4-y+y)^{3}-\\frac{1}{3}(y+y)^{3}]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({4}^{3}-(2y)^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(64-8{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{[64y-2{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}(128-32) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-92fcb5de-d0cd-5bb2-911a-0615ed463dd0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-92fcb5de-d0cd-5bb2-911a-0615ed463dd0" :answer-field/id #uuid "92fcb5de-d0cd-5bb2-911a-0615ed463dd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-48289cb0-2db9-541c-ba9b-d4327439a579" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ee5a9688-f2d5-553e-872b-13b2824acaba" "answer-ce683808-6c11-54ae-bb49-f99568096871" "answer-48289cb0-2db9-541c-ba9b-d4327439a579" "answer-626f8019-c00b-5e2b-9eae-917eb16fcd3d" "answer-77cd1431-7dea-5816-88cc-589a8ce57085"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee5a9688-f2d5-553e-872b-13b2824acaba" :answer/id #uuid "ee5a9688-f2d5-553e-872b-13b2824acaba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce683808-6c11-54ae-bb49-f99568096871" :answer/id #uuid "ce683808-6c11-54ae-bb49-f99568096871" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48289cb0-2db9-541c-ba9b-d4327439a579" :answer/id #uuid "48289cb0-2db9-541c-ba9b-d4327439a579" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-626f8019-c00b-5e2b-9eae-917eb16fcd3d" :answer/id #uuid "626f8019-c00b-5e2b-9eae-917eb16fcd3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77cd1431-7dea-5816-88cc-589a8ce57085" :answer/id #uuid "77cd1431-7dea-5816-88cc-589a8ce57085" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162118 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f125a564-9e7e-50c1-b77c-f6cbd0ae6169" "question-9ba35bb1-196e-51b8-b71e-102fe895702c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f125a564-9e7e-50c1-b77c-f6cbd0ae6169" :question/id #uuid "f125a564-9e7e-50c1-b77c-f6cbd0ae6169" :question/math-academy-id "q-143879" :question/problem "Find $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}+{Y}^{2}],$ given that random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}xy,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables, and $f(x,y)$ is their joint probability density function. If $r:{R}^{2}\\to R$ is a function of two variables, then the rule of the lazy statistician states that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X,Y)]={∬}_{{R}^{2}}r(x,y)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nr(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonzero only in the rectangular region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2\\}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}+{Y}^{2}] & ={∬}_{{R}^{2}}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot xy\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{3}y+x{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{y{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{3}{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{y}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{8}]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+2-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-719de611-fe3d-510b-8ec3-a7dea6d0ecc5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-719de611-fe3d-510b-8ec3-a7dea6d0ecc5" :answer-field/id #uuid "719de611-fe3d-510b-8ec3-a7dea6d0ecc5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cfcead82-4acf-5200-8fd5-75bb552b7196" :answer-field/choices ["answer-67d3f414-e5a3-5a85-86ff-7be8a7d0d430" "answer-b6768082-39bc-5d53-bad6-15fd36ca45b1" "answer-58ac6aa4-3187-51f4-8986-37a77eb9556e" "answer-cfcead82-4acf-5200-8fd5-75bb552b7196" "answer-6ddc4b8b-fe6b-5cab-a0b5-82d769645de3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-67d3f414-e5a3-5a85-86ff-7be8a7d0d430" :answer/id #uuid "67d3f414-e5a3-5a85-86ff-7be8a7d0d430" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b6768082-39bc-5d53-bad6-15fd36ca45b1" :answer/id #uuid "b6768082-39bc-5d53-bad6-15fd36ca45b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58ac6aa4-3187-51f4-8986-37a77eb9556e" :answer/id #uuid "58ac6aa4-3187-51f4-8986-37a77eb9556e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cfcead82-4acf-5200-8fd5-75bb552b7196" :answer/id #uuid "cfcead82-4acf-5200-8fd5-75bb552b7196" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ddc4b8b-fe6b-5cab-a0b5-82d769645de3" :answer/id #uuid "6ddc4b8b-fe6b-5cab-a0b5-82d769645de3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162405 :question/problem "Find $\\text{E}[{X}^{3}(Y+1)],$ given that random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}},\\, & 1\\le x\\le 3,\\,1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables, and $f(x,y)$ is their joint probability density function. If $r:{R}^{2}\\to R$ is a function of two variables, then the rule of the lazy statistician states that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X,Y)]={∬}_{{R}^{2}}r(x,y)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nr(x,y)={x}^{3}(y+1).\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonzero only in the rectangular region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 3,\\,1\\le y\\le 2\\}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{3}(Y+1)] & ={∬}_{{R}^{2}}{x}^{3}(y+1)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{3}(y+1)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{3}(y+1)\\cdot \\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y(y+1){\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y(y+1){[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}4y(y+1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{4{y}^{3}}{3}+2{y}^{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & ={[\\frac{4{y}^{3}}{3}+2{y}^{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{32}{3}+8)-(\\frac{4}{3}+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{46}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186159632 :answer-field/correct 17592186159637 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-9ba35bb1-196e-51b8-b71e-102fe895702c" :question/id #uuid "9ba35bb1-196e-51b8-b71e-102fe895702c" :question/math-academy-id "q-143884" :question/problem "Find $\\text{E}[{e}^{X-Y}],$ given that random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{y},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables, and $f(x,y)$ is their joint probability density function. If $r:{R}^{2}\\to R$ is a function of two variables, then the rule of the lazy statistician states that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X,Y)]={∬}_{{R}^{2}}r(x,y)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nr(x,y)={e}^{x-y}.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonzero only in the rectangular region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{e}^{X-Y}] & ={∬}_{{R}^{2}}{e}^{x-y}\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{e}^{x-y}\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x-y}\\cdot {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}[{e}^{x}]_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(e-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[(e-1)y]_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =(e-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b806adf7-55c6-5e96-8591-27f8f3de0558"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b806adf7-55c6-5e96-8591-27f8f3de0558" :answer-field/id #uuid "b806adf7-55c6-5e96-8591-27f8f3de0558" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a5bb0ace-70a3-52eb-95ec-8d06773149b5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a5bb0ace-70a3-52eb-95ec-8d06773149b5" "answer-fda9eb6e-8342-5d4d-a8b8-51e569d33bde" "answer-419508b7-b598-5bac-aefc-71912a4034c8" "answer-b2538d50-74dd-5675-80ce-ae08eaba9106" "answer-52e29e0e-3acf-5e78-b135-92a31a0d1a0a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5bb0ace-70a3-52eb-95ec-8d06773149b5" :answer/id #uuid "a5bb0ace-70a3-52eb-95ec-8d06773149b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(e-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fda9eb6e-8342-5d4d-a8b8-51e569d33bde" :answer/id #uuid "fda9eb6e-8342-5d4d-a8b8-51e569d33bde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(e-1)^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-419508b7-b598-5bac-aefc-71912a4034c8" :answer/id #uuid "419508b7-b598-5bac-aefc-71912a4034c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2538d50-74dd-5675-80ce-ae08eaba9106" :answer/id #uuid "b2538d50-74dd-5675-80ce-ae08eaba9106" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e-1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-52e29e0e-3acf-5e78-b135-92a31a0d1a0a" :answer/id #uuid "52e29e0e-3acf-5e78-b135-92a31a0d1a0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-2cd388bd-d3e4-5270-8c71-7d4eecc1b15e" :activity/id #uuid "2cd388bd-d3e4-5270-8c71-7d4eecc1b15e" :activity/title "The Rule of the Lazy Statistician for Two Random Variables" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050368 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-45242d45-bd36-5121-80cd-9ac928d0a8f1" "step-8cf947ae-27ad-584f-9aba-1879a81641dc" "step-9e2158cb-c797-5395-8f29-3423911f68bf" "step-813ce03b-2bc9-56d9-bce8-95ab823f7304" "step-2059c6c7-dfef-5a9d-83eb-99b192520566"] :activity/first-step "step-45242d45-bd36-5121-80cd-9ac928d0a8f1" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-45242d45-bd36-5121-80cd-9ac928d0a8f1" :step/id #uuid "45242d45-bd36-5121-80cd-9ac928d0a8f1" :step/content "question-da99206a-ee96-54b9-a8bb-1c95438c5559" :step/next "step-8cf947ae-27ad-584f-9aba-1879a81641dc" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-8cf947ae-27ad-584f-9aba-1879a81641dc" :step/id #uuid "8cf947ae-27ad-584f-9aba-1879a81641dc" :step/content "question-9a19ca23-6c60-5d6e-8799-38d55529cc16" :step/next "step-9e2158cb-c797-5395-8f29-3423911f68bf" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-9e2158cb-c797-5395-8f29-3423911f68bf" :step/id #uuid "9e2158cb-c797-5395-8f29-3423911f68bf" :step/content "question-f125a564-9e7e-50c1-b77c-f6cbd0ae6169" :step/next "step-813ce03b-2bc9-56d9-bce8-95ab823f7304" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-813ce03b-2bc9-56d9-bce8-95ab823f7304" :step/id #uuid "813ce03b-2bc9-56d9-bce8-95ab823f7304" :step/content 17592186162405 :step/next "step-2059c6c7-dfef-5a9d-83eb-99b192520566" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-2059c6c7-dfef-5a9d-83eb-99b192520566" :step/id #uuid "2059c6c7-dfef-5a9d-83eb-99b192520566" :step/content "question-9ba35bb1-196e-51b8-b71e-102fe895702c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-da99206a-ee96-54b9-a8bb-1c95438c5559" :question/id #uuid "da99206a-ee96-54b9-a8bb-1c95438c5559"] ["question-da99206a-ee96-54b9-a8bb-1c95438c5559" :question/math-academy-id "q-143850"] ["question-da99206a-ee96-54b9-a8bb-1c95438c5559" :question/problem "Find $\\text{E}[4(X-1)],$ given that random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4},\\, & 1\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le {x}^{2}; \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-da99206a-ee96-54b9-a8bb-1c95438c5559" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables, and $f(x,y)$ is their joint probability density function. If $r:{R}^{2}\\to R$ is a function of two variables, then the rule of the lazy statistician states that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X,Y)]={∬}_{{R}^{2}}r(x,y)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=4(x-1).\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch the region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le {x}^{2}\\},$ where $f(x,y)$ is nonzero.\n\n![](images/bd/bd8d2d36a0fe570e6ccdb096c6c39bc9c9edeed9b008dada504801025055438f.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[4(X-1)] & ={∬}_{{R}^{2}}4(x-1)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}4(x-1)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{{x}^{2}}4(x-1)\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{2}(x-1){\\int }_{1}^{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{2}(x-1)[y]_{y=1}^{y={x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{2}(x-1)({x}^{2}-1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{2}({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+x]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =3[(4-\\frac{8}{3}-2+2)-(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}+1)] \\\\  & =3(\\frac{4}{3}-\\frac{5}{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-da99206a-ee96-54b9-a8bb-1c95438c5559" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-4a370ffb-9f03-59b2-ac60-62d599bab917" :answer-field/id #uuid "4a370ffb-9f03-59b2-ac60-62d599bab917"] ["answer-d153fc31-a51b-5ff0-a56d-5400a28d1dca" :answer/id #uuid "d153fc31-a51b-5ff0-a56d-5400a28d1dca"] ["answer-d153fc31-a51b-5ff0-a56d-5400a28d1dca" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d153fc31-a51b-5ff0-a56d-5400a28d1dca" :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}"] ["answer-0b87866d-7ca3-5ffe-9bf1-7ca2dbed6087" :answer/id #uuid "0b87866d-7ca3-5ffe-9bf1-7ca2dbed6087"] ["answer-0b87866d-7ca3-5ffe-9bf1-7ca2dbed6087" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0b87866d-7ca3-5ffe-9bf1-7ca2dbed6087" :answer/value "\\frac{13}{4}"] ["answer-0094f649-619d-53d4-bd4a-599974a79f65" :answer/id #uuid "0094f649-619d-53d4-bd4a-599974a79f65"] ["answer-0094f649-619d-53d4-bd4a-599974a79f65" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0094f649-619d-53d4-bd4a-599974a79f65" :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["answer-88871071-0592-5a72-9ee4-9896fb71c1b1" :answer/id #uuid "88871071-0592-5a72-9ee4-9896fb71c1b1"] ["answer-88871071-0592-5a72-9ee4-9896fb71c1b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-88871071-0592-5a72-9ee4-9896fb71c1b1" :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["answer-617c7900-1787-5067-bf53-b914ea33d964" :answer/id #uuid "617c7900-1787-5067-bf53-b914ea33d964"] ["answer-617c7900-1787-5067-bf53-b914ea33d964" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-617c7900-1787-5067-bf53-b914ea33d964" :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}"] ["answer-field-4a370ffb-9f03-59b2-ac60-62d599bab917" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-4a370ffb-9f03-59b2-ac60-62d599bab917" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-4a370ffb-9f03-59b2-ac60-62d599bab917" :answer-field/correct "answer-d153fc31-a51b-5ff0-a56d-5400a28d1dca"] ["answer-field-4a370ffb-9f03-59b2-ac60-62d599bab917" :answer-field/choices "answer-d153fc31-a51b-5ff0-a56d-5400a28d1dca"] ["answer-field-4a370ffb-9f03-59b2-ac60-62d599bab917" :answer-field/choices "answer-0b87866d-7ca3-5ffe-9bf1-7ca2dbed6087"] ["answer-field-4a370ffb-9f03-59b2-ac60-62d599bab917" :answer-field/choices "answer-0094f649-619d-53d4-bd4a-599974a79f65"] ["answer-field-4a370ffb-9f03-59b2-ac60-62d599bab917" :answer-field/choices "answer-88871071-0592-5a72-9ee4-9896fb71c1b1"] ["answer-field-4a370ffb-9f03-59b2-ac60-62d599bab917" :answer-field/choices "answer-617c7900-1787-5067-bf53-b914ea33d964"] ["question-da99206a-ee96-54b9-a8bb-1c95438c5559" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-4a370ffb-9f03-59b2-ac60-62d599bab917"] [17592186162120 :knowledge-point/questions "question-da99206a-ee96-54b9-a8bb-1c95438c5559"] ["question-9a19ca23-6c60-5d6e-8799-38d55529cc16" :question/id #uuid "9a19ca23-6c60-5d6e-8799-38d55529cc16"] ["question-9a19ca23-6c60-5d6e-8799-38d55529cc16" :question/math-academy-id "q-143871"] ["question-9a19ca23-6c60-5d6e-8799-38d55529cc16" :question/problem "Find $\\text{E}[{(X+Y)}^{2}],$ given that random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4},\\, & y\\le x\\le 4-y,\\,0\\le y\\le 2; \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-9a19ca23-6c60-5d6e-8799-38d55529cc16" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables, and $f(x,y)$ is their joint probability density function. If $r:{R}^{2}\\to R$ is a function of two variables, then the rule of the lazy statistician states that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X,Y)]={∬}_{{R}^{2}}r(x,y)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=(x+y)^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch the region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\le x\\le 4-y,\\,0\\le y\\le 2\\},$ where $f(x,y)$ is nonzero.\n\n![](images/8d/8d1935944ffa0017da736fc540ff823df8a052c2c32c985553cde08ea5fce8da.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{(X+Y)}^{2}] & ={∬}_{{R}^{2}}(x+y)^{2}\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(x+y)^{2}\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y}^{4-y}(x+y)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{3}(x+y)^{3}]}_{x=y}^{x=4-y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[\\frac{1}{3}(4-y+y)^{3}-\\frac{1}{3}(y+y)^{3}]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({4}^{3}-(2y)^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(64-8{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{[64y-2{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}(128-32) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-9a19ca23-6c60-5d6e-8799-38d55529cc16" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-92fcb5de-d0cd-5bb2-911a-0615ed463dd0" :answer-field/id #uuid "92fcb5de-d0cd-5bb2-911a-0615ed463dd0"] ["answer-ee5a9688-f2d5-553e-872b-13b2824acaba" :answer/id #uuid "ee5a9688-f2d5-553e-872b-13b2824acaba"] ["answer-ee5a9688-f2d5-553e-872b-13b2824acaba" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ee5a9688-f2d5-553e-872b-13b2824acaba" :answer/value "16"] ["answer-ce683808-6c11-54ae-bb49-f99568096871" :answer/id #uuid "ce683808-6c11-54ae-bb49-f99568096871"] ["answer-ce683808-6c11-54ae-bb49-f99568096871" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ce683808-6c11-54ae-bb49-f99568096871" :answer/value "4"] ["answer-48289cb0-2db9-541c-ba9b-d4327439a579" :answer/id #uuid "48289cb0-2db9-541c-ba9b-d4327439a579"] ["answer-48289cb0-2db9-541c-ba9b-d4327439a579" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-48289cb0-2db9-541c-ba9b-d4327439a579" :answer/value "8"] ["answer-626f8019-c00b-5e2b-9eae-917eb16fcd3d" :answer/id #uuid "626f8019-c00b-5e2b-9eae-917eb16fcd3d"] ["answer-626f8019-c00b-5e2b-9eae-917eb16fcd3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-626f8019-c00b-5e2b-9eae-917eb16fcd3d" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["answer-77cd1431-7dea-5816-88cc-589a8ce57085" :answer/id #uuid "77cd1431-7dea-5816-88cc-589a8ce57085"] ["answer-77cd1431-7dea-5816-88cc-589a8ce57085" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-77cd1431-7dea-5816-88cc-589a8ce57085" :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}"] ["answer-field-92fcb5de-d0cd-5bb2-911a-0615ed463dd0" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-92fcb5de-d0cd-5bb2-911a-0615ed463dd0" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-92fcb5de-d0cd-5bb2-911a-0615ed463dd0" :answer-field/correct "answer-48289cb0-2db9-541c-ba9b-d4327439a579"] ["answer-field-92fcb5de-d0cd-5bb2-911a-0615ed463dd0" :answer-field/choices "answer-ee5a9688-f2d5-553e-872b-13b2824acaba"] ["answer-field-92fcb5de-d0cd-5bb2-911a-0615ed463dd0" :answer-field/choices "answer-ce683808-6c11-54ae-bb49-f99568096871"] ["answer-field-92fcb5de-d0cd-5bb2-911a-0615ed463dd0" :answer-field/choices "answer-48289cb0-2db9-541c-ba9b-d4327439a579"] ["answer-field-92fcb5de-d0cd-5bb2-911a-0615ed463dd0" :answer-field/choices "answer-626f8019-c00b-5e2b-9eae-917eb16fcd3d"] ["answer-field-92fcb5de-d0cd-5bb2-911a-0615ed463dd0" :answer-field/choices "answer-77cd1431-7dea-5816-88cc-589a8ce57085"] ["question-9a19ca23-6c60-5d6e-8799-38d55529cc16" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-92fcb5de-d0cd-5bb2-911a-0615ed463dd0"] [17592186162120 :knowledge-point/questions "question-9a19ca23-6c60-5d6e-8799-38d55529cc16"] ["question-f125a564-9e7e-50c1-b77c-f6cbd0ae6169" :question/id #uuid "f125a564-9e7e-50c1-b77c-f6cbd0ae6169"] ["question-f125a564-9e7e-50c1-b77c-f6cbd0ae6169" :question/math-academy-id "q-143879"] ["question-f125a564-9e7e-50c1-b77c-f6cbd0ae6169" :question/problem "Find $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}+{Y}^{2}],$ given that random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}xy,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-f125a564-9e7e-50c1-b77c-f6cbd0ae6169" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables, and $f(x,y)$ is their joint probability density function. If $r:{R}^{2}\\to R$ is a function of two variables, then the rule of the lazy statistician states that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X,Y)]={∬}_{{R}^{2}}r(x,y)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nr(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonzero only in the rectangular region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2\\}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}+{Y}^{2}] & ={∬}_{{R}^{2}}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot xy\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{3}y+x{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{y{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{3}{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{y}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{8}]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+2-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-f125a564-9e7e-50c1-b77c-f6cbd0ae6169" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-719de611-fe3d-510b-8ec3-a7dea6d0ecc5" :answer-field/id #uuid "719de611-fe3d-510b-8ec3-a7dea6d0ecc5"] ["answer-67d3f414-e5a3-5a85-86ff-7be8a7d0d430" :answer/id #uuid "67d3f414-e5a3-5a85-86ff-7be8a7d0d430"] ["answer-67d3f414-e5a3-5a85-86ff-7be8a7d0d430" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-67d3f414-e5a3-5a85-86ff-7be8a7d0d430" :answer/value "1"] ["answer-b6768082-39bc-5d53-bad6-15fd36ca45b1" :answer/id #uuid "b6768082-39bc-5d53-bad6-15fd36ca45b1"] ["answer-b6768082-39bc-5d53-bad6-15fd36ca45b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b6768082-39bc-5d53-bad6-15fd36ca45b1" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["answer-58ac6aa4-3187-51f4-8986-37a77eb9556e" :answer/id #uuid "58ac6aa4-3187-51f4-8986-37a77eb9556e"] ["answer-58ac6aa4-3187-51f4-8986-37a77eb9556e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-58ac6aa4-3187-51f4-8986-37a77eb9556e" :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["answer-cfcead82-4acf-5200-8fd5-75bb552b7196" :answer/id #uuid "cfcead82-4acf-5200-8fd5-75bb552b7196"] ["answer-cfcead82-4acf-5200-8fd5-75bb552b7196" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-cfcead82-4acf-5200-8fd5-75bb552b7196" :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["answer-6ddc4b8b-fe6b-5cab-a0b5-82d769645de3" :answer/id #uuid "6ddc4b8b-fe6b-5cab-a0b5-82d769645de3"] ["answer-6ddc4b8b-fe6b-5cab-a0b5-82d769645de3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6ddc4b8b-fe6b-5cab-a0b5-82d769645de3" :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}"] ["answer-field-719de611-fe3d-510b-8ec3-a7dea6d0ecc5" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-719de611-fe3d-510b-8ec3-a7dea6d0ecc5" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-719de611-fe3d-510b-8ec3-a7dea6d0ecc5" :answer-field/correct "answer-cfcead82-4acf-5200-8fd5-75bb552b7196"] ["answer-field-719de611-fe3d-510b-8ec3-a7dea6d0ecc5" :answer-field/choices "answer-67d3f414-e5a3-5a85-86ff-7be8a7d0d430"] ["answer-field-719de611-fe3d-510b-8ec3-a7dea6d0ecc5" :answer-field/choices "answer-b6768082-39bc-5d53-bad6-15fd36ca45b1"] ["answer-field-719de611-fe3d-510b-8ec3-a7dea6d0ecc5" :answer-field/choices "answer-58ac6aa4-3187-51f4-8986-37a77eb9556e"] ["answer-field-719de611-fe3d-510b-8ec3-a7dea6d0ecc5" :answer-field/choices "answer-cfcead82-4acf-5200-8fd5-75bb552b7196"] ["answer-field-719de611-fe3d-510b-8ec3-a7dea6d0ecc5" :answer-field/choices "answer-6ddc4b8b-fe6b-5cab-a0b5-82d769645de3"] ["question-f125a564-9e7e-50c1-b77c-f6cbd0ae6169" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-719de611-fe3d-510b-8ec3-a7dea6d0ecc5"] [17592186162118 :knowledge-point/questions "question-f125a564-9e7e-50c1-b77c-f6cbd0ae6169"] [17592186162405 :question/problem "Find $\\text{E}[{X}^{3}(Y+1)],$ given that random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}},\\, & 1\\le x\\le 3,\\,1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186162405 :question/worked-solution "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables, and $f(x,y)$ is their joint probability density function. If $r:{R}^{2}\\to R$ is a function of two variables, then the rule of the lazy statistician states that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X,Y)]={∬}_{{R}^{2}}r(x,y)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nr(x,y)={x}^{3}(y+1).\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonzero only in the rectangular region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 3,\\,1\\le y\\le 2\\}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{3}(Y+1)] & ={∬}_{{R}^{2}}{x}^{3}(y+1)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{3}(y+1)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{3}(y+1)\\cdot \\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y(y+1){\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y(y+1){[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}4y(y+1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{4{y}^{3}}{3}+2{y}^{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & ={[\\frac{4{y}^{3}}{3}+2{y}^{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{32}{3}+8)-(\\frac{4}{3}+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{46}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186162405 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [17592186159632 :answer-field/correct 17592186159637] ["question-9ba35bb1-196e-51b8-b71e-102fe895702c" :question/id #uuid "9ba35bb1-196e-51b8-b71e-102fe895702c"] ["question-9ba35bb1-196e-51b8-b71e-102fe895702c" :question/math-academy-id "q-143884"] ["question-9ba35bb1-196e-51b8-b71e-102fe895702c" :question/problem "Find $\\text{E}[{e}^{X-Y}],$ given that random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{y},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-9ba35bb1-196e-51b8-b71e-102fe895702c" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables, and $f(x,y)$ is their joint probability density function. If $r:{R}^{2}\\to R$ is a function of two variables, then the rule of the lazy statistician states that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X,Y)]={∬}_{{R}^{2}}r(x,y)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nr(x,y)={e}^{x-y}.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonzero only in the rectangular region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{e}^{X-Y}] & ={∬}_{{R}^{2}}{e}^{x-y}\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{e}^{x-y}\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x-y}\\cdot {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}[{e}^{x}]_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(e-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[(e-1)y]_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =(e-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-9ba35bb1-196e-51b8-b71e-102fe895702c" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-b806adf7-55c6-5e96-8591-27f8f3de0558" :answer-field/id #uuid "b806adf7-55c6-5e96-8591-27f8f3de0558"] ["answer-a5bb0ace-70a3-52eb-95ec-8d06773149b5" :answer/id #uuid "a5bb0ace-70a3-52eb-95ec-8d06773149b5"] ["answer-a5bb0ace-70a3-52eb-95ec-8d06773149b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a5bb0ace-70a3-52eb-95ec-8d06773149b5" :answer/value "(e-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] ["answer-fda9eb6e-8342-5d4d-a8b8-51e569d33bde" :answer/id #uuid "fda9eb6e-8342-5d4d-a8b8-51e569d33bde"] ["answer-fda9eb6e-8342-5d4d-a8b8-51e569d33bde" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-fda9eb6e-8342-5d4d-a8b8-51e569d33bde" :answer/value "\\frac{(e-1)^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}"] ["answer-419508b7-b598-5bac-aefc-71912a4034c8" :answer/id #uuid "419508b7-b598-5bac-aefc-71912a4034c8"] ["answer-419508b7-b598-5bac-aefc-71912a4034c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-419508b7-b598-5bac-aefc-71912a4034c8" :answer/value "\\frac{1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}"] ["answer-b2538d50-74dd-5675-80ce-ae08eaba9106" :answer/id #uuid "b2538d50-74dd-5675-80ce-ae08eaba9106"] ["answer-b2538d50-74dd-5675-80ce-ae08eaba9106" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b2538d50-74dd-5675-80ce-ae08eaba9106" :answer/value "\\frac{e-1}{4}"] ["answer-52e29e0e-3acf-5e78-b135-92a31a0d1a0a" :answer/id #uuid "52e29e0e-3acf-5e78-b135-92a31a0d1a0a"] ["answer-52e29e0e-3acf-5e78-b135-92a31a0d1a0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-52e29e0e-3acf-5e78-b135-92a31a0d1a0a" :answer/value "e+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] ["answer-field-b806adf7-55c6-5e96-8591-27f8f3de0558" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-b806adf7-55c6-5e96-8591-27f8f3de0558" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-b806adf